nd more  efficient Crisis Core reunion also  improves one of the original game's most  notable features the digital mind wave  also referred to as the DMW it's a  constantly spinning slot machine style  combat enhancer that lurks in the upper  left corner of your screen during combat  the icons featured on the slots are  characters and summons you meet  throughout the game with characters  providing you limit breaks based on  Zack's relationship to them and summons  granting you the ability to well summon  them as your relationships with certain  characters are altered you become more  or less likely to see them make an  appearance in the DMW in theory it's an  incredibly strange feature as this slot  machine is responsible for allowing you  to dish out your hardest hitting moves  as well as level up in execution however  the DMW is extremely fun and satisfying  generally working out fairly well for  players while also introducing an  element of Randomness to battles that  keep them fresh in the original Crisis  Core this feature did earn some  criticism for its modulating phase which  would grind battles to a halt as the  slots took up the entire screen these  phases no longer exist though Crisis  Core reunion will still interrupt  battles to show brief cutscenes when the  slots land on certain characters  considering the time we get with Zach is  so brief I found these cutscenes not  only fascinating to watch but needed as  an extroverted person who is supremely  devoted to the people around him just  take a look at how many text messages  the guy gets having this mechanic where  Zack's relationships play a role on his  mental state 8 and subsequently the way  he battles is a brilliant choice that  tells us a lot about him without adding  hours on the crisis core's story all  these unique qualities created tangible  difference in Final Fantasy VII and  crisis core's gameplay which drives just  how different Zach and Cloud truly are  Crisis Core also features Mater