e your car along the way  aside from racking up stacks of cash  each of these events also catches the  attention of the local police force If  You're Busted by the cops before making  it back to a safe house you lose all  your winnings and must move on to the  next day adding tension to each running  with the law Need for Speed heat adopted  a similar structure but while the game  featured legal street races throughout  the day and illegal street races at  night Unbound takes the illicit Route 24  7. this means there's no respite from  the police's attention and any money you  make during sunlight hours needs to be  banked at the safe house before you can  transition to the evening's races your  heat level carries over two and only  resets once you're done for the night so  it's up to you how much police presence  you want to accumulate throughout the  day before the sun disappears Over the  Horizon night events tend to feature  significantly higher payouts but they  often require particular levels of heat  or a sizable buy-in if you want to  participate you can still earn money  taking on smaller events but the  increased risk of the larger events  comes with a big cash prize so you're  forced to weigh your options when  deciding on what to do on a day-to-day  basis these decisions are more impactful  during the early game when the cars are  driving aren't quite up to Snuff Unbound  is surprise surprisingly challenging in  his first few hours and I appreciate how  hard it makes you work to achieve  Victory you're competing against drivers  that are simply faster than you racing  in souped-up cars that your initial  junker just can't keep up with you begin  by butting heads with those at the back  of the pack but you can place a bed at  the start of each race that you'll  finish above a certain driver giving you  the chance to earn some extra cash while  setting a Target to beat even if you're  not competing for first place eventually  as the money starts to flow in